    "media:imagetext": "DETROIT\n30)\nROSTON\n•\nCINCINNAT\n- 47)\nWASHINGTON.\nKNOXVILLE\n60\nAN FRANCISCO\n63)\nLOS ANCELES\nSAN ANTONIO\nHACKSONVILI\nMEXICO CITY\nJOWN FISCHER\nWe Shine where the Sun does!\nOfficial Weather Bureau figures show\nsummer sunshine all winter long\non the Southern Route of the Flagships\nIndicates number of days with sunshine during the three winter months\nJusT cance at our Route Map and you me hermany sunny\nand partly sunny days you can expect from December through\nFebruary along the southern \"Sunshine Route\" that Flagships\ntake. These figures are based on official Weather Bureau records.\nSo, if you like to follow the sun on your winter vacation, you'll\nprobably find it beaming from the moment you step aboard your\nFlagship. No wonder American Airlines is the first choice of\ntravelers bound for California, Mexico or the Sun Country.\nOur route, as you can see, is not only clear but clearly con-\nvenient. From coast to coast American goes to most of the places\nthat people want to go, stops at most of the sights that people\nwant to see. And friendly Flagship service makes every moment\nof your journey as bright and enjoyable\nas the sunshine around vou\nAmericas Leading Airline AMERICAN AIRLINES INC.\nReprint of 4-color spread advertisement appearing in Saturday Evening Post, October 28th; Life, November 6th and Time, November 6th.",
